The shopkeeper puts the raincoat in the bag.
I want to go out of the shop.
But before leaving, my eyes fall on a shirt.
It is a cotton shirt.
There are attractive patterns on that shirt.
"Brother, please show this shirt too," I tell the shopkeeper.
He hands me the shirt.
This shirt is more beautiful than the others.
Today there is extreme humidity and heat in Mumbai.
Because of the heat, I am very tired.
Therefore, I do not go to the fitting room.
I do not try the shirt on here.
"I am buying this too," I say.
"Its price is five hundred rupees," the shopkeeper says.
I give him five hundred rupees.
He gives the shirt and the paper receipt.
I place the receipt and the shirt in the bag.
Now I go home quickly by bus.
